        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We talked about this a long time ago, and I know it would be a great move to take over the mobile market, but it doesn't seem to be all that realistic if you think about making a complete VRChat client for mobile devices, since it can barely get the work done on PC. \n\nHowever, there may be an alternative. I think that maybe, just maybe, it would be possible to arrange communication between regular VRChat clients and mobile devices by providing mobile users with voice transmission during 360 live-streaming from a single point based on the location of your friend's holopad or something like that. In my concept, it would require additional power from the PC of the user hosting your call, but I'm sure it would be way easier than porting the whole client, and people would still stay satisfied.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
